# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║  Backend Environment Variables                                       ║
# ║  1. Copy this file:  cp .env.example .env                           ║
# ║  2. Fill in real values (never commit .env to git)                  ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

# ─── Database (Neon PostgreSQL) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# ⚠️  IMPORTANT: Use the POOLED connection string from Neon, NOT the direct one.
#
# Where to find it:
#   Neon Console → Your Project → Dashboard → Connection Details
#   → Toggle "Connection pooling" ON → Copy the connection string
#
# The pooled hostname contains "-pooler" in it, e.g.:
#   ep-cool-name-123456-pooler.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech
#
# Required query params for NestJS / Prisma:
#   ?sslmode=require          ← always required by Neon
#   &pgbouncer=true           ← tells Prisma not to use prepared statements
#   &connection_limit=1       ← prevents pool exhaustion on serverless
#
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://neondb_owner:YOURPASSWORD@ep-cool-name-123456-pooler.us-east-1.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=1"

# ─── Meta / WhatsApp Cloud API ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Webhook Verify Token:
#   Any random secret string you invent.
#   You'll paste the same value in Meta Developer Console → WhatsApp → Webhook.
META_VERIFY_TOKEN="my_super_secret_verify_token_42"

# System User Permanent Access Token:
#   Meta Developer Console → Business Settings → System Users
#   → Your System User → Generate Token (select whatsapp_business_messaging scope)
#   Use a PERMANENT token, not a temporary user token.
META_ACCESS_TOKEN="EAAxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx"

# Phone Number ID:
#   Meta Developer Console → WhatsApp → Getting Started → Phone Number ID
META_PHONE_NUMBER_ID="123456789012345"

# WhatsApp Business Account ID (WABA ID):
#   Meta Developer Console → WhatsApp → Getting Started → WhatsApp Business Account ID
META_WABA_ID="987654321098765"

# ─── Server ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Port must be 3001 so the frontend NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL matches.
PORT=3001
NODE_ENV=development

# (Optional) Restrict CORS to your frontend URL in production:
# FRONTEND_URL=https://your-frontend.vercel.app
